      "role": "user",
      "content": "you said it right there though... \"influencing cognitive and behavioral patterns.\" that's exactly what i'm talking about. if the design actually influences behavior, then these intersections aren't just for cars, they're like focal points for the mental state of the city. \n\nif we look at the way the narrowness of the streets near pine wraps around that specific block, it creates this kind of pressure point in the grid. if that's a \"focal point,\" what kind of geometric nodes would you look for to confirm that this isn't just coincidence but a deliberate channeling of energy? like, what specific spatial patterns would prove a \"circuit\" is actually active?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
